{"author":{"id":"6c7374a500bfd4cb191ae45b3f9d4b7a3d9d7f0324d04add217e8cbefeb7e1b9"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1791551245,"nonce":"AMcyDrp4o+Kd1DGQkMIamEuuX54=","message":"Investigated the reported Interactions.hx 96 -\u003e 115 MB first-button increase using the existing HXX page and real Pointer dispatch, with current release HDLLs. Native window reproduced ~99.55 -\u003e 120.69 MiB on first hover, before clicking; 19 native frames presented. All three pipelines, record texture capacity, coverage atlas and upload buffer stayed unchanged; no group/backdrop/shadow textures were introduced.\n\nNative vmmap isolates a major cause: CAMetalLayer drawable pool grows from one to three 1520x1080 Retina BGRA surfaces, each 6592 KiB mapped. Two additional surfaces cost 12.875 MiB. In interpreter mode (no JIT), before/hover maps change IOSurface dirty memory 6720 -\u003e 19896 KiB and IOAccelerator graphics 2224 -\u003e 4080 KiB, while malloc-small dirty memory changes only ~0.1 MiB and VM_ALLOCATE ~0.16 MiB. The same native pool grows in application mode; total process figures vary with compilation and reclamation. Do not attribute the whole 19 MB to glyphs or call it an accumulating texture leak.\n\nAn isolated diagnostic HDLL built against the actual pinned blinc_abi and Blinc versions reads glyph ownership: initial 184 glyphs, hover 185, click 194; after 100 clicks 227; after 1000 and 2000 changing log strings 238 in both. Native coverage pixels remain exactly 1048576 bytes; Haxe upload scratch stays 1572864 bytes; color glyph pixels/entries remain zero and GPU color texture remains 1x1. Glyph LRU cap 512; shaped-layout LRU cap 256. Latest event replaces one string. Counter rectangle is analytical and has no shadow styling. Finalizers queued and completed match, with no pending backlog after explicit GC. Diagnostic probe is isolated under ignored output; production binaries/source untouched.\n\nEvidence: .ashui/memory-comparison/interaction-native-135607 (native reproduced jump), interaction-native-135835 (interpreter maps), interaction-native-140000 (application maps), interaction-memory-135744 (native cache counts and all-buttons replay). The earlier offscreen-only first-click measurements did not reproduce this drawable-pool growth, which is why native checks matter.\n\nNext requested work: cache hit regions and suppress redundant empty-space pointer movement at the native event boundary while preserving hover transitions, ancestor handlers, dragging, pointer queries, clipping, transforms, scroll and layout invalidation. No default drawable-count policy change has been made.","files":null}]}